      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is right on today\u0027s main, but 1260816 splits `validate` into `validate_structure` and `validate_limits`, and `validate` then runs both. Inlining can push a valid module past a size limit, which 1260816 counts as no optimiser bug, so `vali-opt` asserts only `validate_structure`. Once both changes are in, this `expect` turns an oversized optimised module into a fuzz crash. Whichever lands second should switch this to `vali_dist::validate_structure`. CI won\u0027t flag it, since nothing builds `fuzz/` there.",
      "revId": "3391e39e091e7dc35ab4138ffa279acdfaf19d84",
