      "side": 1,
      "message": "With `NoSource`, every library here is one of Vali\u0027s own, so the mutated artifact loads with `own` set. That\u0027s the trusted path: it skips the `%`-primitive and native-link checks on the code and its transformers (`links_internal`, and the `Binding::Primitive` rule in `check_export`). Those checks are exactly what an untrusted artifact meets, since `own` comes from the loader and an artifact can\u0027t claim it. Mutated transformer code can also reach internal primitives that no user artifact could link.\n\nA second mode would cover the untrusted path: compile a small user library from a `Map`-style loader once, at startup, with `write: true`, and mutate its artifact\u0027s sections the same way. It could be picked by a bit of the input, so one corpus covers both.",
      "revId": "3391e39e091e7dc35ab4138ffa279acdfaf19d84",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
